    "commit_message": "command_bus: remove dead executor_needs_restart rule + resolve 4 orphaned requests\n\nThe Telegram alert this fixes: \"Executor Down \u2014 4 request(s) queued\" /\n\"Auto-restart attempted: FAILED \u2014 Unit telegram-build-executor.service not\nfound.\" That service was intentionally deleted in d98a4207 (this session,\ndead-code removal of the Telegram approval pipeline) - but command_bus.py's\n_rule_executor_needs_restart kept polling for it and firing every cycle.\nExactly the decommissioning gap the drift-check council flagged: the\nwatchdog wasn't retired alongside the thing it watched.\n\nRemoved the rule, _restart_executor(), the now-unreferenced restart log/\ncooldown constants, and _should_act()/_mark_acted() (only ever called by\nthis rule). Rule 1 (executor_stuck) and Rule 2 (service_health) are\nuntouched - neither references the retired service.\n\nDeleted the stale open bus_events row (first_seen 2026-08-29, 2 prior\nnotifications) so nothing lingers waiting for a rule that no longer runs.\n\nSeparately (Supabase, not in this commit): the 4 queued build_request_inbox\nrows were all from 2026-06-18 - legacy source=telegram approvals with no\naction_type and no execution-attempt record, per build_request_verifier.py's\nown vocabulary for this exact case. Nothing has processed these in 2+\nmonths and nothing ever will now. Marked engineering_failed with a\nstructured action_result explaining why, rather than leaving them queued\nforever with no path to resolution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01F1KgvHcPTh7uQNNPDtxRuj",
